  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_003 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc. Multiprofile with avgpool clearly outperforms singleprofile (0.523) and transformer aggregation (0.573). The only untested variation on this exact architecture is the fusion strategy: config_008 swaps weighted fusion for concat fusion while keeping all other settings identical (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile). This isolates a single variable and directly tests whether concatenating the two modality representations (preserving full information) beats their weighted sum. It is the cheapest logical extension of the current best, with expected cost comparable to config_003 (~10–11 GPU hours, similar multiprofile avgpool pipeline). Under the limited budget (6 experiments remaining), this targeted exploitation of the strongest configuration maximizes the chance of finding an incremental improvement without spending GPU hours on a large architectural jump."
